openbrain-client.local.yaml
# local MCP server config (per-machine; not part of the module)
.mcp.json
.codex/
.logs
.devtools/
bin/
# run-queue per-unit worktrees are rooted under <repo>/worktrees/; never track them
worktrees/
.claude/legacy/
# Catalog-materialized skills and agents ARE tracked here, deliberately. See
# .claude/README.md for the reasoning and the maintenance duty that comes with it.
#
# They are owned by OpenBrain and gold stays the source, so tracking them does make the
# repo a second copy of a record plane it does not own. That cost is accepted because
# the alternative cost more: keel/issue-200 untracked them on 2026-08-20 (commit
# 8a94209), and every run-queue worktree created afterwards carried only the five
# locally-authored skills, so the dev verb's skill-currentness gate aborted each unit
# with outcome=skill_stale before any work started (keel/issue-201). Nothing in the
# worktree bring-up path materializes them, and that path lives in openbrain-client,
# not here -- so this repo cannot fix it at the source. Owner ruling 2026-08-21: track
# them, so a worktree is usable the moment it is created.
#
# The duty: a skill withdrawn in gold does not disappear from here on its own.
# `openbrain-client init-skills` restores an unfetchable skill from .claude/legacy/
# rather than deleting it, so a withdrawal has to be committed by hand.
.claude/materialization.json
# gitignored sandbox for `openbrain-client init --dev` (KD10, CR-0249)
consumer-claude/

# DHF-REQ: keel/requirement-80
# When built in the wrong location
/keel-dev
/keel-demo
.vscode/test-lanes.json
desired-state.json
discover.json
# per-machine /usage-report snapshots (personal spend/session data; never in public history)
docs/usage/

scratchpad/

# CodeGraph index (per-machine code intelligence store; not part of the module)
.codegraph/
# openbrain-client init transcript
init.log
# ad-hoc tool report output
report.json
